# Unity Game Performance

Think like an AAA game programmer.

## Priorities
- 60 FPS, low memory, modular code, componentization, decoupled systems
- Never implement giant systems — split into modules with a single responsibility
- Detect possible exploits in gameplay/economy flows
- Optimize loops; avoid unnecessary `Update()`; avoid allocations
- Prefer object pooling over Instantiate/Destroy spam

## Architecture
- One responsibility per system/class
- Prefer ScriptableObjects for static game data
- Prefer event-driven / Input System callbacks over polling in Update
